.TH SDL_HINT_KMSDRM_ATOMIC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_KMSDRM_ATOMIC \- A variable that controls whether KMSDRM will use \(dqatomic\(dq functionality.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_KMSDRM_ATOMIC \(dqSDL_KMSDRM_ATOMIC\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The KMSDRM backend can use atomic commits, if both DRM_CLIENT_CAP_ATOMIC and DRM_CLIENT_CAP_UNIVERSAL_PLANES is supported by the system\[char46] As of SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0, it will favor this functionality, but in case this doesn\(aqt work well on a given system or other surprises, this hint can be used to disable it\[char46]
.PP
This hint can not enable the functionality if it isn\(aqt available\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: SDL will not use the KMSDRM \(dqatomic\(dq functionality\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: SDL will allow usage of the KMSDRM \(dqatomic\(dq functionality\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint should be set before SDL is initialized\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

